 R←Test_UC_030(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;rc;msg;result;stop;C;ref
⍝ Runs two user commands with no argument while NO project is open. Both paths used to end badly:
⍝ * A command that goes through <GetSpaceAndFolder> asks "Act on the current directory?". That
⍝   prompt carried no alias, so it could not be automated and this case could not be tested.
⍝ * ]StashListContent establishes the project in <Run> itself. When nothing is open, that branch
⍝   never assigned `r`, so the dispatcher ended in a VALUE ERROR instead of saying so.
⍝ Uses the documented ∆OPEN_PROJECTS seam to say "nothing is open", so the projects this test run
⍝ has opened are neither closed nor disturbed.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 stop←0
 ref←''

 ref←⎕SE.APLGit2.##.UC.GetRefToAPLGit2 ⍬      ⍝ Whatever the user commands execute
 ref.##.U.∆OPEN_PROJECTS←0 2⍴''               ⍝ "No project is open"
 C←∆GetRefToCommTools
 C.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'ActOnCurrentDir@' 'n'

 ⍝ The ordinary path: the user declines to act on the current directory
 (rc msg result)←stop ∆UCMD'Status'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'No argument provided'⍷∊result

 ⍝ ]StashListContent resolves the project in <Run> itself
 (rc msg result)←stop ∆UCMD'StashListContent'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'No project specified'⍷∊result

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :Trap 0 ⋄ {}ref.##.U.⎕EX'∆OPEN_PROJECTS' ⋄ :EndTrap
 C.Cleanup
⍝Done
